# Enchiladas

Based on multiple recipes, like this one: [https://12tomatoes.com/spinach-and-cheese-enchilada/…](https://12tomatoes.com/spinach-and-cheese-enchiladas) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251204100718/https://12tomatoes.com/spinach-and-cheese-enchiladas))

{ rating="5" image="enchiladas.jpg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### Core Ingredients

- [ ] [Rotisserie chicken]{ ing="rotisserie-chicken" }
- [ ] [Burrito size Tortillas]{ ing="burrito-size-tortillas" }
- [ ] 1-2 cans of [enchilada sauce]{ ing="enchilada-sauce" } (~20 oz)
- [ ] 1 or 2 cans of [black beans]{ ing="black-beans" }, strained
- [ ] Can of [diced green chilies]{ ing="diced-green-chilies" }
- [ ] 1/2 lb[. Shredded Mexican cheese]{ ing="shredded-mexican-cheese" }
- [ ] [Sour cream]{ ing="sour-cream" } (or cottage cheese), for serving
- [ ] (Optional) 1/2 cup cottage cheese mixed [into the filling]{ ing="into-the-filling" } for extra protein

### Vegetarian Ingredients

The chicken can be substituted with all veggies based on [https://cookieandkate.com/vegetarian-enchiladas-recipe/…](https://cookieandkate.com/vegetarian-enchiladas-recipe) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251116083100/https://cookieandkate.com/vegetarian-enchiladas-recipe/))

- [ ] 6 oz (5 cups) [baby spinach]{ ing="baby-spinach" }
- [ ] 1 [red onion]{ ing="red-onion" }, diced
- [ ] 1 [red bell pepper]{ ing="red-bell-pepper" }, chopped
- [ ] 1 lb of [broccoli or cauliflower]{ ing="broccoli-or-cauliflower" }, remove florets and slice into bite-size pieces
- [ ] 1 tsp [Ground Cumin]{ ing="ground-cumin" }
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [Ground Cinnamon]{ ing="ground-cinnamon" }

## Recipe

### Core Recipe

1. Bake the [chicken]{ ing="rotisserie-chicken" } (if not already cooked)
1. Preheat the oven to 375F
1. Roll the cooked chicken, [cheese]{ ing="shredded-mexican-cheese" }, [beans]{ ing="black-beans" }, and other vegetables into burritos. Place flap side down and then pour [enchilada sauce]{ ing="enchilada-sauce" } over top
1. Bake for 25 minutes

### Vegetarian Recipe

1. In a large skillet over medium heat, saute the [onions]{ ing="red-onion" } in olive oil (5-7 min)
1. Add broccoli and [bell pepper]{ ing="red-bell-pepper" }. Reduce heat to medium-low and cover. Cook for 8 min
1. Add the [cumin]{ ing="ground-cumin" } and [cinnamon]{ ing="ground-cinnamon" }
1. Add the [spinach]{ ing="baby-spinach" } in handfuls and heat until all wilted
1. Spoon into each enchilada in place of the chicken
